WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.567
AGORA — How was the euro born and what does it mean for Romania?

2
00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:13.233
Bolta — What did the sky above you look like, in any place and on any day between 1900 and 2100?

3
00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:19.900
Cupa Mondială 2026 — Play at the 2026 World Cup and watch an imaginary tournament unfold.

4
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:26.567
Eclipsa din 2 august 2027 — See on a map where and for how long the total solar eclipse of 2 August 2027 lasts, with cities and place search, without internet.

5
00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:33.233
Horizons — Travel through the history of the universe from the Big Bang to the end, in 91 milestones.

6
00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:39.900
Hyper4D — See what four-dimensional shapes look like: rotate them on screen and view them from several angles.

7
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:46.567
IncredibleCosmos — Place planets and stars so that their gravity guides a comet to the target.

8
00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:53.233
Nemurirea — Discover how the body ages and what science says about biological clocks and longevity, then test yourself with a quiz.

9
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:59.900
ORARIUM — What time is it now on Mars, on the Moon or on an asteroid?

10
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:06.567
TerRa — A 3D globe and a map showing day and night on Earth, the Moon and the planets.

11
00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:13.233
Universul Observabil — How big is the Universe we can see?

12
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:19.900
Universul Observabil 1D — Start from us and travel toward the edge of the visible Universe, passing 112 galaxies placed on a single axis.

13
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.567
Universul Observabil 2D — A map of galaxies in the satirical "Flat Earth" edition: a joke, the Earth is not flat.

14
00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:33.233
Universul Observabil 3D — Fly among over 115 galaxies on a 3D map, with guided tours and challenges.

15
00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:39.900
VietAR — Photograph or record a plant or creature and get an idea of the species, out of 519 from Romania.
